    source: 'startupjobs',
    company: 'Sudolabs',
    description:
      "<p><strong>Type of contract:</strong> full-time or trade license</p><p><strong>Place of work:</strong> Kosice or remote</p><p><strong>Start date:</strong> let us know what time suits you best</p><p><strong>Compensation:</strong> from €15/hour up to €30/hour</p><p>At Sudolabs we are expanding our technology team. We're looking for TypeScript&nbsp;developers, who have relevant experience with React and Node.js. You will work in a team of 3-5 engineers using agile development processes, always working on a single project at a time. Prepare for detailed code reviews and pair programming.</p><p><strong>As an engineer, we expect you to:</strong></p><ul><li><p>be responsible for estimating and shipping epics and smaller projects,</p></li><li><p>help teammates and share knowledge with them,</p></li><li><p>have deeper knowledge and experience with some technology or have big picture knowledge and experience across the full-stack (web/mobile, backend, infrastructure),</p></li><li><p>have an understanding of your domain/project and make decisions based on business needs,</p></li><li><p>sometimes communicate technical stuff with the client or product manager,</p></li><li><p>sometimes research new trends and technologies,</p></li><li><p>contribute to knowledge-base.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Who are we looking for?</strong></p><ul><li><p>TypeScript&nbsp;developers, who have relevant experience with React and Node.js.</p></li><li><p>Code quality is one of the most important things for us, so we expect you to care about the code you write.</p></li><li><p>Product-oriented thinking.</p></li><li><p>The ability to work independently, as well as in a team environment.</p></li><li><p>You should be eager to learn new things and improve your skills.</p></li><li><p>We’re expecting you to be open-minded, share feedback, and spread knowledge to other team members, contributing to our knowledge-base and from time to time to organize discussions, and events.</p></li><li><p>Resident of the Slovak or Czech Republic, Slovak/Czech at a communicative level.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Benefits and perks</strong></p><p>Once you check our career pages, you can get a clear sense of how we work, what our values are, and what we can offer. Among many benefits, we would like to highlight a few:</p><ul><li><p>Permanent contract or trade license - choose what fits you</p></li><li><p>Possibility to work from our office in Kosice or from wherever you like</p></li><li><p>20 paid days/year in your work time to learn new things</p></li><li><p>31 paid days/year time off</p></li><li><p>Flexible working hours</p></li><li><p>Internal tech talks on a regular basis</p></li><li><p>Hardware package - MacBook or anything you need</p></li><li><p>Team buildings&nbsp;</p></li><li><p>Sudo apartment in Kosice - for our remote colleagues who would like to spend some time with us in Kosice</p></li><li><p>Possibility to purchase a Multisport card</p></li><li><p>Brand new office in the city center with parking space</p></li><li><p>Pet-friendly office</p></li><li><p>Regular snacks are a must, of course!</p></li></ul>",
