      '<section><div><strong>Description<br><br></strong>Sécheron Hasler Group continues the Swiss tradition of over 140 years in the field of railway technology. We are a leading global supplier of electrical and electronic safety components and solutions and traction power systems for the railway industry and also provide solutions for renewable energy, DC grid, and other industrial systems. The name Sécheron Hasler Group is a worldwide synonym for Swiss Quality and represents a leading reference for state of the art products supplied to the market.<br><br>With more than 1’200 employees worldwide, we are wherever our customers are around the globe, supplying products approved in our customers’ countries or markets and deliver top-notch supply chain and customer services locally.<br><br>For our <strong>Traction Power Systems site in Prague</strong>, we are looking for a <strong>Mechanical Design Engineer</strong> to strengthen our engineering team.<br><br>Projects are typically smaller in scope, tailored to specific customer requirements and focused on <strong>configuration and engineering changes of existing solutions</strong>.<br><br>The goal is always the same: deliver a solution that is <strong>technically correct, manufacturable and ready for implementation.<br><br></strong><strong>In This Role, You Will<br><br></strong><ul><li> Design mechanical parts and assemblies using 3D CAD (SolidWorks)</li><li>Create complete manufacturing and assembly documentation, including drawings for suppliers</li><li>Adapt and configure existing mechanical solutions for customer projects</li><li>Work on engineering and change requests across several smaller projects in parallel</li><li>Maintain and manage technical data in ERP system (Oracle)</li><li>Cooperate closely with electrical and software engineers, production, purchasing, quality and project management</li><li>Support projects throughout execution and implementation </li><li>Communicate regularly with the team and customers in English<br><br></li></ul><strong>Requirements<br><br></strong><strong>What are we looking for:<br><br></strong><ul><li>High school or university degree in Mechanical Engineering</li><li>At least 3 years of experience in mechanical design / engineering</li><li>Solid understanding of mechanical design principles</li><li>Strong experience with 3D CAD systems (SolidWorks preferred)</li><li>Ability to work independently and take responsibility for assigned tasks</li><li>Comfortable working on multiple smaller projects rather than one long R&amp;D assignment</li><li>Fluent English (main working language) and Czech </li><li>Basic knowledge of electrical engineering would be a strong advantage<br><br></li></ul>If you do not meet every single point but feel this role fits your mindset and interests, we encourage you to apply.<br><br><strong>Benefits<br><br></strong><strong>What we offer<br><br></strong><ul><li>A stable and interesting engineering position with visible, real‑world impact</li><li>Work in a supportive team and company with great reputation</li><li>Cooperation with customers across the world and exposure to global projects</li><li>Opportunities to learn, grow and build your technical expertise through hands‑on project work</li><li>Flexible working hours</li><li>Attractive benefits package including 13th salary, transport allowance, meal vouchers and pension contribution</li><li>5 weeks of vacation and additional benefits<br><br></li></ul>If you are looking for an engineering role where your work is practical, varied and actually delivered to customers, we would be happy to hear from you.<br><br>Sécheron Hasler Group is committed to creating a diverse and inclusive environment and welcomes applications from all qualified candidates. </div><button> Show more <icon></icon></button><button> Show less <icon></icon></button></section>',
